{"answers":[],"asked":[{"category":"errors","id":"Q-9","impact":1,"impactReason":"This affects work planning, not product behavior or user-visible flows.","options":["Approve all 25 requirements as one run.","Keep the full scope and split it across three runs.","Reject this scope and identify requirements to cut."],"reason":"This preserves the requested full scope without adding a split or cutting requested work.","recommended":"Approve all 25 requirements as one run.","score":3,"spans":[],"text":"How should the 25-requirement scope be handled for this run?","uncertainty":3}],"checks":{"critic":[{"finding":"REQ-8 never says what the list operation returns for an unsupported or malformed status filter value, so this error path has no defined response and no AC.","reqId":"REQ-8","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-16 blocks duplicate create calls, but REQ-19 does not say whether the status action is disabled while pending, so a double-click can send a second, disallowed transition and show the REQ-20 error even though the first change succeeded.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"If a status update is rejected because the stored status changed elsewhere, REQ-20 still keeps the previously displayed status and action with no refresh, so the screen stays out of sync with the stored status.","reqId":"REQ-20","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-3 trims the description, but no requirement says whether a description that is blank after trimming is stored as absent (so 'No description.' shows) or as an empty string, which leaves REQ-2's 'only if one was supplied' and REQ-18 ambiguous.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-14.2 depends on a 'missing area' state, but REQ-13 never says whether the Area select starts empty or has a placeholder (only Priority gets a default), so that state may not be reachable in the UI.","reqId":"REQ-14","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-2.1, AC-5.1, AC-6.1, AC-6.2, AC-7.2 and the AC-10.x criteria all assert on the 'persisted row' or 'database row', which is internal storage rather than a public API or UI surface.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-1.1 and AC-1.2 say navigation 'shows only' two screens and 'the screen list contains no third screen', but the app has no observable screen list, so a test cannot check the absence of other screens.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-7.2 expects edit or delete attempts to be 'rejected', but REQ-7 says those operations do not exist and never defines the rejection response (for example, 404/405), or what happens to title or area fields included in a change-status call.","reqId":"REQ-7","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The intent is tagged auth/pii risk and ASM-2 hosts the app in the client's cloud, yet no requirement says how the unauthenticated API is access-controlled, so anyone who can reach it can create requests and change statuses.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The demo user identity 'Sam Carter' / 'SC' is hardcoded in REQ-1 and REQ-11, and no intent span sources it, instead of coming from configuration.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-6 does not specify creation timestamps for the seed rows, so if they all share one timestamp the newest-first seeded list order is unspecified (per Q-3), which weakens the ordering checks in AC-8.1 and AC-12.1.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-18 retains the previously selected filter on Back, but it does not say what the filter should be when the detail address was opened directly with no prior list visit, or whether the list refetches to show a status changed on the detail screen.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-21.3 only checks that another load request is sent, not that the screen shows the request after a successful retry, so the user-visible outcome i