","sources":["I-4","I-5","Q-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The creation dialog is open while a filter other than All is selected.","id":"AC-15.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the dialog closed, All selected, and the new Open request at the top of the list.","when":"The user submits valid values and the API creates the request."}],"ears":"When request creation succeeds, the Hive Works app shall close the dialog and show the new Open request at the top of the list, switching the selected filter to All if another filter was selected.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The creation dialog contains valid values and the create request is pending.","id":"AC-16.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the Create button disabled and the API receives only 1 create call for that submission.","when":"The user attempts to submit again before the request completes."},{"given":"The API returns a non-validation creation failure.","id":"AC-16.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows a generic creation error, retains the dialog and entered field values, and allows another submission.","when":"The user submits the creation dialog."}],"ears":"The Hive Works app shall disable the Create button and prevent duplicate create calls while a create request is being sent, and, after a non-validation creation failure, show a generic creation error while keeping the dialog and entered values open and allowing another submission.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-4"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The list request is pending, returns no matching requests, or fails to load.","id":"AC-17.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows “Loading requests…” while pending, “No requests here.” when empty, or “Could not load requests.” with a Retry button on failure.","when":"The Requests screen renders each respective state."},{"given":"The Requests screen shows the load error and Retry button.","id":"AC-17.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned request list.","when":"The user selects Retry and loading succeeds."}],"ears":"While the request list is loading, empty for the selected filter, or unavailable, the Hive Works app shall show the corresponding loading, empty, or error state and provide Retry for the error state.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A request with a description is opened from the list.","id":"AC-18.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the request fields, badges, date-only creation date, description, and Back link.","when":"The detail screen renders."},{"given":"A request without a description is opened from the list.","id":"AC-18.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows “No description.” and a Back link.","when":"The detail screen renders."},{"given":"A status filter was selected before a request was opened.","id":"AC-18.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the Requests list with the previously selected filter still selected.","when":"The user follows the detail screen's Back link."}],"ears":"The Hive Works Request detail screen shall show a Back link, the request title, area, priority badge, status badge, UTC creation date in date-only form, and the description or “No description.” when absent, and return to the Requests list with its previously selected filter retained when Back is followed.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-8"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A request is displayed with each of the statuses Open, In progress, or Done.","id":"AC-19.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows Start work, Mark done, or Reopen respectively, and after a successful response the status badge and action button show the new status and next action.","when":"The detail screen renders and the user selects its status action, with the API confirming the change."}],"ears":"The Hive Works Request detail screen shall show Start work for Open requests, Mark done for In progress requests, and Reopen for Done requests, and update the status badge and action button only after a successful status-change response.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The detail screen shows a request with a known status.","id":"AC-20.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows “Could not update the request.” and the status badge and action button retain their previous values.","when":"The API returns a failure for the status update."}],"ears":"If a status update fails, then the Hive Works app shall show “Could not update the request.” and keep the previously displayed status and action unchanged.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The detail screen is opened with an unknown ID.","id":"AC-21.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows “Request not found.” and a link back to the Requests screen.","when":"The ID lookup completes."},{"given":"The detail screen is opened with a known ID and loading fails for a non-not-found reason.","id":"AC-21.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows a generic loading error and a Retry action, not “Request not found.”.","when":"The load failure is returned."},{"given":"The detail screen shows a generic loading error.","id":"AC-21.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen sends another request to load the detail address.","when":"The user selects Retry."}],"ears":"The Hive Works app shall show “Request not found.” with a link back to the Requests screen for an unknown ID, and show a generic loading error with Retry but not “Request not found.” when loading a known ID fails for another reason.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-5"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The Requests and request detail screens are rendered with all badge types and primary buttons.","id":"AC-22.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the light theme, neutral background, near-black text, sans-serif font, one primary-button brand color, and the specified status and priority badge colors, with each badge showing its status or priority value.","when":"Their theme and badges are inspected."}],"ears":"The Hive Works app shall use one light theme with a neutral background, near-black text, one primary-button brand color, one sans-serif font, Open blue badges, In progress amber badges, Done green badges, Urgent red badges, and neutral Low and Normal badges, with text on every badge.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The Requests, creation dialog, and detail screens are rendered at 375 px and 1280 px viewport widths.","id":"AC-23.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows stacked request cards at 375 px, a request table at 1280 px, no horizontal page scroll, labels for every field, and keyboard-reachable controls.","when":"The screens and controls are inspected and navigated by keyboard."}],"ears":"The Hive Works app shall present labeled fields and keyboard-reachable controls on both screens and provide stacked request cards at 375 px and a request table at 1280 px viewport widths without horizontal page scrolling.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6","I-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The automated business-rule test suite is available.","id":"AC-24.1","level":"job","then":"The test report lists passing cases for a valid request starting Open, missing or too-short title, missing area, too-long description, each allowed status transition, a disallowed transition, a status-filtered newest-first list, and an unknown ID.","when":"The suite is run against the application API."}],"ears":"The Hive Works project shall include automated tests for request creation and validation, all allowed and disallowed status transitions, filtered newest-first listing, and unknown-ID handling.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The app is available to the end-to-end test.","id":"AC-25.1","level":"ui","then":"The test report shows the workflow passed and the screen shows the created request in the Done list.","when":"The test opens the list, creates a request, opens it, selects Start work and Mark done, then filters by Done."}],"ears":"The Hive Works project shall include an end-to-end test for the create, detail, status-change, and filter workflow.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8"],"stability":1}]}}